# Own-wording spells of Grim Hollow Player's Guide (2014 rules), part A. TEXT = {name: [summary, full]}.
HL = "\n\n**At Higher Levels.** "
TEXT = {
"Arboreal Curse": ["60 ft, until dispelled. Constitution save or Restrained as flesh turns to bark. Three failed saves make the target a tree.",
 "60 ft, until dispelled. You try to turn a creature you see into wood. If its body is flesh, it makes a Constitution save. On a success nothing happens. On a failure it is Restrained as its flesh hardens. It repeats the save at the end of each of its turns. Three successes end the spell. Three failures turn it into a tree and it is Petrified for the duration. The saves need not be consecutive, so track both counts. If the tree is burned, felled or destroyed, the creature dies. Remove curse, wish or similar magic can undo the change within one year. After a year and a day as a tree, the change is permanent."],
"Blood Bond": ["Touch, 1 hour. Spend three Hit Dice. The target gains temporary hit points equal to the roll and you share a telepathic link.",
 "Touch, 1 hour. You must spend three Hit Dice to cast this, or the spell fails. Roll them. The target gains that many temporary hit points. While the spell lasts you always know the target's direction and distance, you can talk to each other telepathically if it has Intelligence 3 or more, and you can target it with your spells of range Self or Touch. These benefits stop while you are on different planes. The target can end the spell at any time. If it does, it loses the remaining temporary hit points from this spell and takes Necrotic damage equal to the amount lost." + HL + "A 5th or 6th level slot makes the duration 8 hours. A 7th or 8th level slot makes it 24 hours. A 9th level slot makes it 7 days."],
"Blood Rush": ["Self, instant. Spend a Hit Die and regain the roll plus your spellcasting modifier in hit points.",
 "Self. You must spend a Hit Die to cast this, or the spell fails. Roll it and regain hit points equal to the result plus your spellcasting ability modifier." + HL + "For each slot level above 1st you can spend and roll one extra Hit Die."],
"Bloodletter": ["Touch, 1 minute, Concentration. The next creature hit by a touched nonmagical weapon makes a Constitution save or gets a festering wound (2d6 Necrotic each turn).",
 "Touch, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You touch a nonmagical weapon. The next creature it hits must make a Constitution save or take a festering wound. A creature with a festering wound takes 2d6 Necrotic damage at the start of each of its turns while the spell lasts. A creature can have only one wound at a time. Any magical healing of at least 1 hit point closes the wound and stops the damage." + HL + "The wound's damage rises by 1d6 for each slot level above 2nd."],
"Calling Card": ["Touch, until dispelled. Mark a corpse with a visible or invisible magical sign that anyone examining the body for it finds.",
 "Touch, until dispelled. You touch a corpse and leave a magical mark on it. You choose whether it appears as a visible rune or word on the flesh or stays invisible. Any creature that specifically examines the corpse for a calling card finds it automatically, whether visible or not."],
"Circle of Scarlet": ["120 ft, instant. Spend four Hit Dice. A 15-ft radius, 100-ft high pillar deals Necrotic damage equal to the roll, and failing creatures lose four of their own Hit Dice too.",
 "120 ft, instant. You must spend four Hit Dice to cast this, or the spell fails. Choose a point on the ground in range and roll the dice. A crimson pillar erupts there, 15 ft in radius and 100 ft high. Each creature inside makes a Constitution save. On a success it takes Necrotic damage equal to the total. On a failure it takes that damage and must also spend and roll four of its own Hit Dice, taking extra Necrotic damage equal to the result. You gain 5 temporary hit points for each creature that fails."],
"Consume Mind": ["Self, 1 hour. Eat a bit of a corpse's brain to recall facts it knew. Ability check DC equals the corpse's Intelligence.",
 "Self, 1 hour. You eat a portion of the brain of a corpse and gain its memories and knowledge. The corpse needs a brain, cannot be undead, and fails if dead more than three days without preservation. For the duration you can try to recall any important fact the creature knew, such as family history, recent events, layouts, passwords or details of its death. Each attempt is an ability check with your spellcasting modifier against a DC equal to the corpse's Intelligence score. You cannot retry the same fact."],
"Consumption": ["60 ft, 1 minute, Concentration. Spend a Hit Die. The target loses hit points equal to the roll, and again each turn it fails a Constitution save.",
 "60 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You must spend a Hit Die to cast this, or the spell fails. Choose a creature in range and roll the die. It loses that many hit points. At the end of each of its turns it makes a Constitution save. On a failure, roll the same die again and it loses that many hit points. On a success the effect ends for it." + HL + "Choose one more target for each slot level above 1st."],
"Creeping Death": ["60 ft, 1 minute, Concentration. Spend eight Hit Dice to set a death threshold. The target dies if its hit points fall to it or below.",
 "60 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You must spend eight Hit Dice to cast this, or the spell fails. Roll and total them to set the target's creeping death threshold. While the spell lasts, the target dies at once if its current hit points are ever equal to or below that threshold. As a bonus action on each of your turns you can force the target to make a Constitution save. On a failure roll 2d6 and add it to the threshold. On a success add half the roll. After three successful saves, which need not be consecutive, the spell ends."],
"Creeping Touch": ["Self, 10 minutes, Concentration. Your severed hand becomes a spider you control, see through and hear through.",
 "Self, up to 10 minutes, Concentration. You detach your hand at the wrist and it becomes a spider. Within 100 ft you can speak to it telepathically. As an action you can see and hear through it until the start of your next turn, and you are blind and deaf to your own senses meanwhile. If the spider is killed or kept from returning, your hand is restored and you take 1d6 Psychic damage. If you order it back, it crawls to your wrist and the spell ends."],
"Crimson Lash": ["Self, 10 minutes. Spend a Hit Die. A blood whip uses that die for Necrotic damage and cuts the target's hit point maximum.",
 "Self, 10 minutes. You must spend a Hit Die to cast this, or the spell fails. A lash of clotted blood forms in your hand as a magic weapon until the spell ends. It is a simple weapon you are proficient with, with the light, finesse and reach properties. You can use your spellcasting modifier instead of Strength or Dexterity for its attack and damage rolls. Its damage die is the Hit Die you spent and the damage is Necrotic. Each time it damages a creature, that creature's hit point maximum drops by the damage taken." + HL + "With a 3rd or 4th level slot you can make two attacks when you take the Attack action, if both use the lash. With a 5th level or higher slot you can make three."],
"Crown of Radiance": ["Self, 10 minutes. A holy crown sheds light and deals 2d8 Radiant damage to nearby fiends, fey and undead.",
 "Self, 10 minutes. A flaming crown of holy light sits on your head. Any fiend, fey or undead that moves within 20 ft of you, or starts its turn there, takes 2d8 Radiant damage. The crown sheds bright light in a 30-ft radius and dim light for another 30 ft."],
"Dark Sacrament": ["Self, instant. Spend four Hit Dice for a melee spell attack with a jeweled dagger. A kill grants a dark blessing for 10 minutes.",
 "Self, instant. You must spend four Hit Dice to cast this, or the spell fails. Make a melee spell attack with the dagger against a creature within 5 ft. On a hit, roll the spent dice plus 4d8 and deal that much Necrotic damage. If this reduces the creature to 0 hit points, it dies and you gain a dark blessing: Advantage on all saves, your size grows one category, you gain temporary hit points equal to your Constitution modifier (minimum 1) at the start of each of your turns, your weapon attacks deal 1d4 extra damage, and your Proficiency Bonus rises by 2. It ends after 10 minutes or when you drop to 0 hit points. While you have it, Radiant damage deals an extra 1d4 to you." + HL + "The attack's damage rises by 1d8 for each slot level above 4th."],
"Earth Worm": ["60 ft, 1 minute, Concentration. A worm-maw of earth bites for 3d8 plus your modifier and swallows Large or smaller creatures.",
 "60 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You shape the ground into a worm-like maw in an open spot in range. When you cast it you can make a melee spell attack against a creature within 5 ft of it. On a hit the target takes Piercing damage equal to 3d8 plus your spellcasting modifier. A Large or smaller target makes a Dexterity save or is swallowed. A swallowed creature is Blinded and Restrained, has total cover from outside, and takes 6d6 Bludgeoning damage at the start of each of your turns. On its turn it can use an action to repeat the save. On a success it is expelled and falls Prone within 10 ft. As a bonus action you can move the worm 20 ft and attack again against a creature within 5 ft."],
"Fiend Flesh": ["Touch, 1 hour, Concentration. A willing creature gains Resistance to Cold, Fire and Lightning and immunity to Poison damage.",
 "Touch, up to 1 hour, Concentration. You touch a willing creature. Its skin turns red and scaly. For the duration it has Resistance to Cold, Fire and Lightning damage and is immune to Poison damage."],
"Flash Fever": ["60 ft, 1 minute, Concentration. Constitution save or a fever deals 1d6 Fire damage, growing by 1d6 each time you trigger it.",
 "60 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. A living creature you pick in range breaks into a cold sweat and makes a Constitution save. On a success the spell ends. On a failure its fever rises and it takes 1d6 Fire damage at the start of its next turn. While the spell lasts you can use your reaction at the start of the creature's turn to make it take Fire damage again, 1d6 more each time. The creature can use its action to cool itself and repeat the save. On a success the fever breaks and the spell ends." + HL + "The first damage rises by 1d6 for each slot level above 3rd."],
"Flense": ["60 ft, 1 minute, Concentration. Ranged spell attack, then Constitution save for 8d6 Necrotic damage, repeated each turn.",
 "60 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You peel the skin from a creature you see in range with necromantic force. Make a ranged spell attack against it. The target makes a Constitution save, taking 8d6 Necrotic damage on a failure and half on a success. On each of your turns you can use your action to force another save and repeat the damage. The spell ends if the target leaves range, drops to 0 hit points, or gains total cover from you."],
"Ghost Light": ["Touch, 1 hour. An object glows with silver light seen only by creatures you name.",
 "Touch, 1 hour. You touch one object no larger than 10 ft in any dimension and name any number of creatures you see within 10 ft. The object sheds bright silvery light in a 20-ft radius and dim light for another 20 ft. Only the named creatures can see the light. Everyone else sees the area as usual."],
"Heartseeker": ["300 ft, 1 minute, Concentration. Spend six Hit Dice for a blood arrow. It deals Piercing damage and widens the crit range against the target.",
 "300 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You must spend six Hit Dice to cast this, or the spell fails. Blood leaves your body and hardens into a barbed arrow that flies at a creature in range. Make a ranged spell attack. On a hit roll the spent dice and the target takes that much Piercing damage. The arrow then burrows toward its heart. At the start of the target's next turn it makes a Constitution save. On a failure, attacks against it crit on a 19 or 20. At the start of each later turn it repeats the save, and each failure widens the crit range by 1 more. After three successes, which need not be consecutive, the spell ends. The wider range ends with the spell."],
"Hunter Sense": ["Touch, 1 minute, Concentration. A willing target treats a d20 roll of 9 or less as 10 on Wisdom (Perception) checks.",
 "Touch, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You heighten the senses of a willing creature. While the spell lasts, if it rolls 9 or lower on the d20 for a Wisdom (Perception) check, it treats the roll as a 10."],
"Incite Riot": ["30 ft, 1 minute, Concentration. Creatures that see you make a Wisdom save or are Charmed and must brawl with the nearest creature.",
 "30 ft, up to 1 minute, Concentration. You wave a red handkerchief and pick any number of creatures in range that can see you. Each makes a Wisdom save or is Charmed by you until the spell ends or until you or your allies harm it. While Charmed this way it must use its turn to make unarmed strikes against the nearest creature other than you, or to move toward the nearest target. At the end of each of its turns it can repeat the save to end the effect on itself."],
}
